{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:5135-1","published":"2026-11-09T12:56:28Z","modified":"2026-11-10T13:15:10.656423856Z","related":["CVE-2026-100236","CVE-2026-86561","CVE-2026-86563","CVE-2026-86565","CVE-2026-86566","CVE-2026-86845","CVE-2026-86846","CVE-2026-86847","CVE-2026-86848","CVE-2026-86849","CVE-2026-86856","CVE-2026-93683"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-100236","CVE-2026-86561","CVE-2026-86563","CVE-2026-86565","CVE-2026-86566","CVE-2026-86845","CVE-2026-86846","CVE-2026-86847","CVE-2026-86848","CVE-2026-86849","CVE-2026-86856","CVE-2026-93683"],"summary":"Security update for dpdk22","details":"This update for dpdk22 fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-86561: missing memory size validation before mmap in vhost memory region setup (bsc#1285678).\n- CVE-2026-86563: double offset bug in vhost log mapping calculation (bsc#1285676).\n- CVE-2026-86565: split-ring inflight descriptor table overflow (bsc#1285672).\n- CVE-2026-86566: copy length underflow in vhost enqueue (bsc#1285671).\n- CVE-2026-86845: use-after-free and type confusion in vhost-crypto session handling (bsc#1285666).\n- CVE-2026-86846: vhost-crypto TOCTOU out-of-bounds write in finalize path (bsc#1285664).\n- CVE-2026-86847: infinite cleanup loop in vhost-crypto writeback chain (bsc#1285663).\n- CVE-2026-86848: vhost-crypto TOCTOU out-of-bounds write in finalize path (bsc#1285657).\n- CVE-2026-86849: integer overflow and missing validation in vhost-crypto request handling (bsc#1285658).\n- CVE-2026-86856: stack and heap buffer overflow in nfp vDPA driver (bsc#1285659).\n- CVE-2026-93683: indirect descriptor table double-fetch (bsc#1285660).\n- CVE-2026-100236: GSO library heap out-of-bounds read/write with small mbuf pools (bsc#1285679).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"dpdk22","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Micro 5.5","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/dpdk22&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Micro%205.5"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"22.11.11-150500.5